        "type": "the-purpose",
        "title": "Untitled",
        "body": "This topic set explores the intersection of cosmology, stellar astrophysics, and planetary science, tailored for a non-expert audience. The topics move beyond simple definitions to investigate the *processes* that govern the lives of stars and planets. They cover the lifecycle of stars from their birth in nebulae to their dramatic deaths, the fascinating methods used to discover and characterize planets outside our solar system (exoplanets), and the profound connection between stellar death and the chemical ingredients necessary for life. Each topic is designed to be explored in depth, examining its history, underlying principles, observational evidence, and broader significance for understanding our place in the cosmos.",
        "line_number": 23,
        "source": "topic-set-stellar-and-planetary-cosmology-from-birth-to-diversity-🆔20251031025753.md",
        "char_start": 392,
